WEBVTT
Language: en

1
00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:17.367
The bucket starts full at five tokens, and each accepted request spends one. allow(now) adds refill for the time since the last call, so no background timer runs. The chips above are R1–R10 at their arrival times.

2
00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:36.267
Six requests arrive at time zero. No time has passed, so refill adds nothing: the first five spend the balance and the sixth hits the tokens &lt; 1 check and gets 429.

3
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:55.467
Refill is (now − lastRefill) × 2. R7 at 0.5 s gains 1.0 and R8 at 1 s gains 1.0; R9 arrives at the same instant as R8 and gains nothing. R9 (0.0) is under 1 token, so it gets 429.

4
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:10.333
R10 arrives at 2 s, one second after R9, and gains 2.0. The min(5, …) cap keeps the balance at five or below however long a client waits. R10 spends one token and leaves 1.0.

5
00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:26.667
Each bar is the balance left after one allow call, and the red notes sit on the requests that got 429.
